\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. All glory to God in the sky,
\par And peace upon earth be restored!
\par O Jesus, exalted on high,
\par Appear our omnipotent Lord!
\par Who, meanly in Bethlehem born,
\par Didst stoop to redeem a lost race,
\par Once more to Thy creatures return,
\par And reign in Thy kingdom of grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When Thou in our flesh didst appear,
\par All nature acknowledged Thy birth;
\par Arose the acceptable year,
\par And heaven was opened on earth:
\par Receiving its Lord from above,
\par The world was united to bless
\par The Giver of concord and love,
\par The Prince and the Author of peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O wouldst Thou again be made known!
\par Again in Thy Spirit descend,
\par And set up in each of Thine own
\par A kingdom that never shall end.
\par Thou only art able to bless,
\par And make the glad nations obey,
\par And bid the dire enmity cease,
\par And bow the whole world to Thy sway.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Come then to Thy servants again,
\par Who long Thy appearing to know,
\par Thy quiet and peaceable reign
\par In mercy establish below;
\par All sorrow before Thee shall fly,
\par And anger and hatred be o'er,
\par And envy and malice shall die,
\par And discord afflict us no more.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

